{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"tool_nTPSnrwbqD3eHGCUD9PUcIwq","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# SE3 External Controller Architecture\n     2→\n     3→## 问题分析\n     4→\n     5→### 当前架构的痛点\n     6→\n     7→1. **嵌套限制**: `se3 collab --daemon` 在 Claude Code 内部运行时，worker 无法启动（Claude 禁止嵌套）\n     8→2. **提交遗漏**: Claude 没有确定性机制确保提交，依赖自我提醒\n     9→3. **进程管理**: bash orchestrator 功能受限（信号处理、状态恢复困难）\n    10→\n    11→### 根本原因\n    12→\n    13→控制权在 **Claude 内部** → 外部只能通过文件/信号间接控制 → 不可靠\n    14→\n    15→## 新架构：外部控制模型\n    16→\n    17→```\n    18→┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n    19→│                      User Terminal                          │\n    20→│  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐   │\n    21→│  │  $ se3 session start                               │   │\n    22→│  │  [External Controller Daemon starts]               │   │\n    23→│  │  [Auto-commit watcher starts]                      │   │\n    24→│  │  [Claude Process spawned in subprocess]            │   │\n    25→│  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘   │\n    26→└────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────┘\n    27→                     │ stdio/pty\n    28→                     ▼\n    29→┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n    30→│                   Claude Interactive Mode                    │\n    31→│  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐   │\n    32→│  │  User <-> Claude 交互（正常对话模式）               │   │\n    33→│  │  Claude 通过 MCP/文件与 External Controller 通信    │   │\n    34→│  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘   │\n    35→└────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────┘\n    36→                     │ MCP / File System\n    37→                     ▼\n    38→┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n    39→│              External Controller Daemon (Python)            │\n    40→│  ┌─────────────┐  ┌─────────────┐  ┌─────────────────────┐ │\n    41→│  │ Session     │  │ Auto-Commit │  │ Worker Coordinator │ │\n    42→│  │ Manager     │  │ Watcher     │  │ (for collab mode)  │ │\n    43→│  └─────────────┘  └─────────────┘  └─────────────────────┘ │\n    44→│  ┌─────────────┐  ┌─────────────┐                          │\n    45→│  │ Status      │  │ Change      │                          │\n    46→│  │ Persistence │  │ Detector    │                          │\n    47→│  └─────────────┘  └─────────────┘                          │\n    48→└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n    49→```\n    50→\n    51→## 核心组件\n    52→\n    53→### 1. Session Controller (`se3 session`)\n    54→\n    55→```python\n    56→class SessionController:\n    57→    \"\"\"\n    58→    管理单个 Claude 会话的生命周期\n    59→    \"\"\"\n    60→\n    61→    def start(self):\n    62→        # 1. 启动 Claude 作为子进程（交互模式）\n    63→        # 2. 连接 stdio/pty\n    64→        # 3. 启动 auto-commit watcher\n    65→        pass\n    66→\n    67→    def pause(self):\n    68→        # 保存状态，暂停 Claude 进程（非终止）\n    69→        pass\n    70→\n    71→    def resume(self):\n    72→        # 恢复之前的会话状态\n    73→        pass\n    74→\n    75→    def stop(self):\n    76→        # 确保提交后终止\n    77→        pass\n    78→```\n    79→\n    80→#### CLI 接口\n    81→\n    82→```bash\n    83→# 启动新会话\n    84→se3 session start\n    85→\n    86→# 暂停当前会话（保存上下文）\n    87→se3 session pause\n    88→\n    89→# 恢复会话\n    90→se3 session resume\n    91→\n    92→# 强制提交并停止\n    93→se3 session stop --commit\n    94→\n    95→# 查看状态\n    96→se3 session status\n    97→```\n    98→\n    99→### 2. Auto-Commit Watcher\n   100→\n   101→```python\n   102→class AutoCommitWatcher:\n   103→    \"\"\"\n   104→    基于启发式规则的自动提交\n   105→    \"\"\"\n   106→\n   107→    def should_commit(self) -> bool:\n   108→        # 触发条件（满足任一）：\n   109→        # 1. 文件修改后 5 分钟无新修改（静默期）\n   110→        # 2. 测试通过且未提交（se3 commit 会运行测试）\n   111→        # 3. 用户显式发送 /commit 命令\n   112→        # 4. 即将停止会话时（SIGTERM）\n   113→        pass\n   114→\n   115→    def commit_with_message(self):\n   116→        # 使用 AI 生成提交信息（可选）\n   117→        # 或基于修改的文件类型推断\n   118→        pass\n   119→```\n   120→\n   121→### 3. Worker Coordinator (替代 collab --daemon)\n   122→\n   123→```python\n   124→class WorkerCoordinator:\n   125→    \"\"\"\n   126→    在当前 Claude 外部协调多个 Claude 进程\n   127→    解决嵌套限制问题\n   128→    \"\"\"\n   129→\n   130→    def spawn_worker(self, task_id: str):\n   131→        # 启动独立 Claude 进程作为 worker\n   132→        # 通过文件系统/MCP 通信\n   133→        pass\n   134→\n   135→    def spawn_manager(self, event_type: str):\n   136→        # 启动 manager 审核结果\n   137→        pass\n   138→```\n   139→\n   140→## 数据流\n   141→\n   142→### 正常交互流\n   143→\n   144→```\n   145→User Input\n   146→    │\n   147→    ▼\n   148→┌─────────────────┐\n   149→│ se3 session     │\n   150→│ (stdio proxy)   │\n   151→└────────┬────────┘\n   152→         │\n   153→    ┌────┴────┐\n   154→    ▼         ▼\n   155→┌────────┐  ┌──────────────┐\n   156→│ Claude │  │ Auto-Commit  │\n   157→│ Process│  │ Watcher      │\n   158→└───┬────┘  │ (file watch) │\n   159→    │       └──────┬───────┘\n   160→    │              │\n   161→    │  modifies    │ detects\n   162→    │  files       │ silence\n   163→    │              │\n   164→    └──────────────┘\n   165→              │\n   166→              ▼\n   167→        ┌──────────┐\n   168→        │ se3 commit│\n   169→        │ (auto)   │\n   170→        └──────────┘\n   171→```\n   172→\n   173→### 协作模式流\n   174→\n   175→```\n   176→External Controller (Daemon)\n   177→    │\n   178→    ├── spawn_manager(\"plan\") → 独立 Claude 进程\n   179→    │                            │\n   180→    │                            ▼\n   181→    │                      [Manager: 生成 tasks]\n   182→    │                            │\n   183→    │◄───────────────────────────┘\n   184→    │\n   185→    ├── spawn_worker(\"task-001\") → 独立 Claude 进程\n   186→    │                               │\n   187→    │                               ▼\n   188→    │                         [Worker: 实现任务]\n   189→    │                               │\n   190→    │◄──────────────────────────────┘\n   191→    │\n   192→    └── spawn_manager(\"review\") → ...\n   193→```\n   194→\n   195→## 关键设计决策\n   196→\n   197→### 1. 为什么用外部 Daemon 而不是当前进程？\n   198→\n   199→| 方案 | 优点 | 缺点 |\n   200→|------|------|------|\n   201→| Claude 内部控制 | 简单 | 嵌套限制、提交遗漏 |\n   202→| 外部 Daemon | 无嵌套限制、确定性提交 | 需要进程间通信 |\n   203→\n   204→### 2. 自动提交触发策略\n   205→\n   206→```python\n   207→COMMIT_TRIGGERS = {\n   208→    # 时间触发\n   209→    \"silence_timeout\": 300,  # 5 分钟无文件修改\n   210→\n   211→    # 事件触发\n   212→    \"tests_pass\": True,      # 测试通过后\n   213→    \"user_command\": \"/commit\",  # 用户显式命令\n   214→    \"session_end\": True,     # 会话结束前强制提交\n   215→\n   216→    # 内容触发\n   217→    \"completed_task\": True,  # progress.md 标记任务完成\n   218→}\n   219→```\n   220→\n   221→### 3. 与现有 collab 的整合\n   222→\n   223→```\n   224→se3 collab --daemon    →    se3 collab start\n   225→                              (由外部 controller 管理)\n   226→\n   227→当前架构：                 新架构：\n   228→bash orchestrator    →    Python daemon\n   229→├─ spawn manager     →    ├─ spawn_claude(\"manager\")\n   230→├─ spawn worker      →    ├─ spawn_claude(\"worker\")\n   231→└─ file events       →    └─ async event loop\n   232→```\n   233→\n   234→## 实现路线图\n   235→\n   236→### Phase 1: Session Controller 基础\n   237→- [ ] `se3 session start/stop/status`\n   238→- [ ] Claude 子进程管理\n   239→- [ ] 基本的 stdio 代理\n   240→\n   241→### Phase 2: Auto-Commit\n   242→- [ ] 文件系统监控（watchdog）\n   243→- [ ] 静默期检测\n   244→- [ ] 自动 `se3 commit` 触发\n   245→\n   246→### Phase 3: Collab 迁移\n   247→- [ ] Worker Coordinator\n   248→- [ ] 独立 Claude 进程启动\n   249→- [ ] 任务状态机\n   250→\n   251→### Phase 4: 增强功能\n   252→- [ ] 会话持久化（崩溃恢复）\n   253→- [ ] 多个并发会话管理\n   254→- [ ] Web UI 监控面板\n   255→\n   256→## MCP 工具设计\n   257→\n   258→Claude 通过 MCP 与外部 Controller 通信：\n   259→\n   260→```python\n   261→# se3-controller MCP server\n   262→\n   263→@mcp.tool()\n   264→def report_task_complete(task_id: str, summary: str):\n   265→    \"\"\"Worker 完成任务时调用\"\"\"\n   266→    pass\n   267→\n   268→@mcp.tool()\n   269→def request_human_input(question: str, urgency: str = \"normal\"):\n   270→    \"\"\"需要人类输入时调用\"\"\"\n   271→    pass\n   272→\n   273→@mcp.tool()\n   274→def trigger_commit(reason: str):\n   275→    \"\"\"Claude 显式请求提交\"\"\"\n   276→    pass\n   277→\n   278→@mcp.tool()\n   279→def spawn_worker_task(task_spec: dict):\n   280→    \"\"\"Claude 请求启动 worker\"\"\"\n   281→    pass\n   282→```\n   283→\n   284→## 与现有代码的兼容性\n   285→\n   286→- `se3 collab` 命令保持不变（内部调用 controller）\n   287→- `.collab/` 目录结构保持不变\n   288→- `scripts/collab-orchestrator.sh` 逐步迁移到 Python daemon\n   289→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"26847e8e-a8cf-4e28-8be2-13f7a7769227","uuid":"1ecc2523-3019-4241-bc49-ec3100952c12","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/data/cre/workspace/se3.0/.worktrees/remove-external-controller/openspec/specs/se3-controller/EXTERNAL-CONTROLLER-ARCH.md","content":"# SE3 External Controller Architecture\n\n## 问题分析\n\n### 当前架构的痛点\n\n1. **嵌套限制**: `se3 collab --daemon` 在 Claude Code 内部运行时，worker 无法启动（Claude 禁止嵌套）\n2. **提交遗漏**: Claude 没有确定性机制确保提交，依赖自我提醒\n3. **进程管理**: bash orchestrator 功能受限（信号处理、状态恢复困难）\n\n### 根本原因\n\n控制权在 **Claude 内部** → 外部只能通过文件/信号间接控制 → 不可靠\n\n## 新架构：外部控制模型\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                      User Terminal                          │\n│  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐   │\n│  │  $ se3 session start                               │   │\n│  │  [External Controller Daemon starts]               │   │\n│  │  [Auto-commit watcher starts]                      │   │\n│  │  [Claude Process spawned in subprocess]            │   │\n│  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘   │\n└────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────┘\n                     │ stdio/pty\n                     ▼\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                   Claude Interactive Mode                    │\n│  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐   │\n│  │  User <-> Claude 交互（正常对话模式）               │   │\n│  │  Claude 通过 MCP/文件与 External Controller 通信    │   │\n│  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘   │\n└────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────┘\n                     │ MCP / File System\n                     ▼\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│              External Controller Daemon (Python)            │\n│  ┌─────────────┐  ┌─────────────┐  ┌─────────────────────┐ │\n│  │ Session     │  │ Auto-Commit │  │ Worker Coordinator │ │\n│  │ Manager     │  │ Watcher     │  │ (for collab mode)  │ │\n│  └─────────────┘  └─────────────┘  └─────────────────────┘ │\n│  ┌─────────────┐  ┌─────────────┐                          │\n│  │ Status      │  │ Change      │                          │\n│  │ Persistence │  │ Detector    │                          │\n│  └─────────────┘  └─────────────┘                          │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n## 核心组件\n\n### 1. Session Controller (`se3 session`)\n\n```python\nclass SessionController:\n    \"\"\"\n    管理单个 Claude 会话的生命周期\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def start(self):\n        # 1. 启动 Claude 作为子进程（交互模式）\n        # 2. 连接 stdio/pty\n        # 3. 启动 auto-commit watcher\n        pass\n\n    def pause(self):\n        # 保存状态，暂停 Claude 进程（非终止）\n        pass\n\n    def resume(self):\n        # 恢复之前的会话状态\n        pass\n\n    def stop(self):\n        # 确保提交后终止\n        pass\n```\n\n#### CLI 接口\n\n```bash\n# 启动新会话\nse3 session start\n\n# 暂停当前会话（保存上下文）\nse3 session pause\n\n# 恢复会话\nse3 session resume\n\n# 强制提交并停止\nse3 session stop --commit\n\n# 查看状态\nse3 session status\n```\n\n### 2. Auto-Commit Watcher\n\n```python\nclass AutoCommitWatcher:\n    \"\"\"\n    基于启发式规则的自动提交\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def should_commit(self) -> bool:\n        # 触发条件（满足任一）：\n        # 1. 文件修改后 5 分钟无新修改（静默期）\n        # 2. 测试通过且未提交（se3 commit 会运行测试）\n        # 3. 用户显式发送 /commit 命令\n        # 4. 即将停止会话时（SIGTERM）\n        pass\n\n    def commit_with_message(self):\n        # 使用 AI 生成提交信息（可选）\n        # 或基于修改的文件类型推断\n        pass\n```\n\n### 3. Worker Coordinator (替代 collab --daemon)\n\n```python\nclass WorkerCoordinator:\n    \"\"\"\n    在当前 Claude 外部协调多个 Claude 进程\n    解决嵌套限制问题\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def spawn_worker(self, task_id: str):\n        # 启动独立 Claude 进程作为 worker\n        # 通过文件系统/MCP 通信\n        pass\n\n    def spawn_manager(self, event_type: str):\n        # 启动 manager 审核结果\n        pass\n```\n\n## 数据流\n\n### 正常交互流\n\n```\nUser Input\n    │\n    ▼\n┌─────────────────┐\n│ se3 session     │\n│ (stdio proxy)   │\n└────────┬────────┘\n         │\n    ┌────┴────┐\n    ▼         ▼\n┌────────┐  ┌──────────────┐\n│ Claude │  │ Auto-Commit  │\n│ Process│  │ Watcher      │\n└───┬────┘  │ (file watch) │\n    │       └──────┬───────┘\n    │              │\n    │  modifies    │ detects\n    │  files       │ silence\n    │              │\n    └──────────────┘\n              │\n              ▼\n        ┌──────────┐\n        │ se3 commit│\n        │ (auto)   │\n        └──────────┘\n```\n\n### 协作模式流\n\n```\nExternal Controller (Daemon)\n    │\n    ├── spawn_manager(\"plan\") → 独立 Claude 进程\n    │                            │\n    │                            ▼\n    │                      [Manager: 生成 tasks]\n    │                            │\n    │◄───────────────────────────┘\n    │\n    ├── spawn_worker(\"task-001\") → 独立 Claude 进程\n    │                               │\n    │                               ▼\n    │                         [Worker: 实现任务]\n    │                               │\n    │◄──────────────────────────────┘\n    │\n    └── spawn_manager(\"review\") → ...\n```\n\n## 关键设计决策\n\n### 1. 为什么用外部 Daemon 而不是当前进程？\n\n| 方案 | 优点 | 缺点 |\n|------|------|------|\n| Claude 内部控制 | 简单 | 嵌套限制、提交遗漏 |\n| 外部 Daemon | 无嵌套限制、确定性提交 | 需要进程间通信 |\n\n### 2. 自动提交触发策略\n\n```python\nCOMMIT_TRIGGERS = {\n    # 时间触发\n    \"silence_timeout\": 300,  # 5 分钟无文件修改\n\n    # 事件触发\n    \"tests_pass\": True,      # 测试通过后\n    \"user_command\": \"/commit\",  # 用户显式命令\n    \"session_end\": True,     # 会话结束前强制提交\n\n    # 内容触发\n    \"completed_task\": True,  # progress.md 标记任务完成\n}\n```\n\n### 3. 与现有 collab 的整合\n\n```\nse3 collab --daemon    →    se3 collab start\n                              (由外部 controller 管理)\n\n当前架构：                 新架构：\nbash orchestrator    →    Python daemon\n├─ spawn manager     →    ├─ spawn_claude(\"manager\")\n├─ spawn worker      →    ├─ spawn_claude(\"worker\")\n└─ file events       →    └─ async event loop\n```\n\n## 实现路线图\n\n### Phase 1: Session Controller 基础\n- [ ] `se3 session start/stop/status`\n- [ ] Claude 子进程管理\n- [ ] 基本的 stdio 代理\n\n### Phase 2: Auto-Commit\n- [ ] 文件系统监控（watchdog）\n- [ ] 静默期检测\n- [ ] 自动 `se3 commit` 触发\n\n### Phase 3: Collab 迁移\n- [ ] Worker Coordinator\n- [ ] 独立 Claude 进程启动\n- [ ] 任务状态机\n\n### Phase 4: 增强功能\n- [ ] 会话持久化（崩溃恢复）\n- [ ] 多个并发会话管理\n- [ ] Web UI 监控面板\n\n## MCP 工具设计\n\nClaude 通过 MCP 与外部 Controller 通信：\n\n```python\n# se3-controller MCP server\n\n@mcp.tool()\ndef report_task_complete(task_id: str, summary: str):\n    \"\"\"Worker 完成任务时调用\"\"\"\n    pass\n\n@mcp.tool()\ndef request_human_input(question: str, urgency: str = \"normal\"):\n    \"\"\"需要人类输入时调用\"\"\"\n    pass\n\n@mcp.tool()\ndef trigger_commit(reason: str):\n    \"\"\"Claude 显式请求提交\"\"\"\n    pass\n\n@mcp.tool()\ndef spawn_worker_task(task_spec: dict):\n    \"\"\"Claude 请求启动 worker\"\"\"\n    pass\n```\n\n## 与现有代码的兼容性\n\n- `se3 collab` 命令保持不变（内部调用 controller）\n- `.collab/` 目录结构保持不变\n- `scripts/collab-orchestrator.sh` 逐步迁移到 Python daemon\n","numLines":289,"startLine":1,"totalLines":289}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"tool_dMyHaIbzQyYXu9kFGH4rwomq","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# git-worktree-collab Specification (v2 - Simplified)\n     2→\n     3→## Purpose\n     4→\n     5→Replace the experimental External Controller (v2) with a simplified architecture based on the proven bash orchestrator (v1). Remove unnecessary complexity: no daemon, no HTTP API, no MCP server, no real-time manager-worker communication.\n     6→\n     7→**Core principle**: Git worktree-based isolation + file-based async communication only.\n     8→\n     9→## Architecture Overview\n    10→\n    11→```\n    12→┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n    13→│  Layer 1: Orchestrator (bash)                       │\n    14→│  - Event loop: spawn → wait → react                 │\n    15→│  - File system is the ONLY communication channel    │\n    16→│  - Zero AI token cost while idle                    │\n    17→├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n    18→│  Layer 2: Manager (claude -p)                       │\n    19→│  - Invoked on-demand when decisions needed          │\n    20→│  - Stateless: reads .collab/, writes decisions      │\n    21→│  - NO real-time communication with workers          │\n    22→├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n    23→│  Layer 3: Workers (claude -p)                       │\n    24→│  - Isolated in git worktrees                        │\n    25→│  - Independent full context window                  │\n    26→│  - Commit & exit — process exit = task complete     │\n    27→└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n    28→```\n    29→\n    30→## Key Design Decisions\n    31→\n    32→### 1. No Daemon, No API, No MCP\n    33→\n    34→**REMOVED from v2:**\n    35→- ❌ Python daemon process (`daemon.py`)\n    36→- ❌ HTTP API server (`api_server.py`)\n    37→- ❌ MCP server for manager-worker communication (`mcp-collab/server`)\n    38→- ❌ Real-time progress reporting\n    39→\n    40→**RATIONALE:**\n    41→- Bash orchestrator is sufficient — it spawns processes and waits for exit\n    42→- File system communication is simpler and more reliable\n    43→- Manager and Worker do NOT need to communicate during worker execution\n    44→- Worker progress is tracked via git commits, not real-time reports\n    45→\n    46→### 2. Async Communication Only\n    47→\n    48→**Communication pattern:**\n    49→```\n    50→Manager creates Task File ──► Worker reads Task File (at start)\n    51→                              Worker works independently\n    52→                              Worker writes result (git commit + exit)\n    53→Worker exit triggers ───────► Manager reads result (at end)\n    54→```\n    55→\n    56→**NO communication during worker execution:**\n    57→- Manager does not monitor worker progress\n    58→- Worker does not ask manager questions mid-task\n    59→- Worker blocks/writes human-calls/ directly if human needed\n    60→\n    61→**RATIONALE:**\n    62→- Git worktree paradigm: branch is isolation boundary\n    63→- Commit history is the progress indicator\n    64→- Human calls go directly to human-calls/, not through manager\n    65→\n    66→### 3. Simplified Health Monitoring\n    67→\n    68→**Worker health:**\n    69→- Process timeout via bash `timeout` command\n    70→- Git commit activity check (orchestrator polls periodically)\n    71→- NO heartbeat/MCP required\n    72→\n    73→**Manager health:**\n    74→- Timeout on `claude -p` invocation\n    75→- JSON validation with retry\n    76→\n    77→**Orchestrator health:**\n    78→- NO watchdog layer — orchestrator crash = session ends\n    79→- State persistence in `.collab/` allows manual resume\n    80→\n    81→## Requirements\n    82→\n    83→### Requirement: Three-Layer Architecture (Simplified)\n    84→\n    85→The system SHALL use a three-layer architecture with bash orchestrator, manager (claude -p), and workers (claude -p).\n    86→\n    87→**Orchestrator** (Layer 1):\n    88→- Pure bash script — no daemon, no resident process\n    89→- Spawns manager/worker via `claude -p`, waits for exit\n    90→- Reads task files, updates status, makes spawn decisions\n    91→- All state in `.collab/` files — orchestrator is stateless\n    92→\n    93→**Manager** (Layer 2):\n    94→- Invoked via `claude -p` for specific decisions only\n    95→- Reads `.collab/` state, returns JSON decision\n    96→- Does NOT communicate with running workers\n    97→- Exits after returning decision\n    98→\n    99→**Workers** (Layer 3):\n   100→- Each runs as independent `claude -p` in git worktree\n   101→- Full context window, no shared state pressure\n   102→- Commits to branch, exits when done (exit code = result)\n   103→- If blocked: write to `human-calls/`, exit with code 2\n   104→\n   105→#### Scenario: Event-driven orchestrator loop\n   106→- **WHEN** orchestrator starts\n   107→- **THEN** it spawns manager for initial planning\n   108→- **WHEN** manager returns task list\n   109→- **THEN** orchestrator spawns workers up to `max_parallel_workers`\n   110→- **WHEN** any worker exits\n   111→- **THEN** orchestrator spawns manager for review/failure-handling\n   112→- **WHEN** all tasks terminal\n   113→- **THEN** orchestrator exits\n   114→\n   115→#### Scenario: Stateless recovery\n   116→- **WHEN** orchestrator is restarted with `--resume`\n   117→- **THEN** it reads `.collab/config.json` and `.collab/tasks/*.json`\n   118→- **AND** resumes the event loop from current state\n   119→\n   120→---\n   121→\n   122→### Requirement: Task File Protocol (Unchanged)\n   123→\n   124→The system SHALL use JSON task files in `.collab/tasks/` as the single source of truth.\n   125→\n   126→**Task lifecycle**: `pending` → `in_progress` → (`done` | `failed` | `blocked` | `timeout`)\n   127→\n   128→**Task file format**: Same as v1 (see original spec for full schema)\n   129→\n   130→Key fields:\n   131→- `id`, `status`, `branch`, `worktree`\n   132→- `prompt`: Full worker prompt\n   133→- `worker_pid`: Set by orchestrator when spawning\n   134→- `worker_exit_code`: Set by orchestrator on exit\n   135→- `health.attempts`: Retry counter\n   136→- `health.timeout_minutes`: Timeout setting\n   137→\n   138→**Collaboration config** (`.collab/config.json`):\n   139→```json\n   140→{\n   141→  \"session_id\": \"collab-20260215-100000\",\n   142→  \"objective\": \"Implement features X, Y, Z\",\n   143→  \"base_branch\": \"master\",\n   144→  \"max_parallel_workers\": 3,\n   145→  \"worker_timeout_minutes\": 60,\n   146→  \"manager_timeout_minutes\": 15,\n   147→  \"status\": \"active\"\n   148→}\n   149→```\n   150→\n   151→#### Scenario: Task persistence\n   152→- **WHEN** orchestrator spawns a worker\n   153→- **THEN** it writes `worker_pid` to task file\n   154→- **WHEN** worker exits\n   155→- **THEN** orchestrator records `worker_exit_code` and updates `status`\n   156→\n   157→---\n   158→\n   159→### Requirement: Manager-Worker Async Boundary\n   160→\n   161→Manager and Worker SHALL NOT communicate during worker execution.\n   162→\n   163→**Worker prompt includes:**\n   164→- Task description\n   165→- Spec references\n   166→- Rules (from `rules-worker.md`)\n   167→- Instruction: \"Work independently. Commit your changes. Exit when done.\"\n   168→\n   169→**Worker blocked/needs help:**\n   170→- Worker writes to `human-calls/` directly\n   171→- Worker exits with code 2 (blocked)\n   172→- Orchestrator sets status to `blocked`\n   173→- Human response processed in next orchestrator loop\n   174→\n   175→**Manager decisions (JSON response):**\n   176→```json\n   177→{\n   178→  \"action\": \"plan|merge|reject|retry|split|escalate|complete\",\n   179→  \"tasks\": [...],\n   180→  \"target_task\": \"task-001\",\n   181→  \"merge_branch\": \"collab/feature-x\",\n   182→  \"retry_prompt\": \"...\",\n   183→  \"reason\": \"...\",\n   184→  \"summary\": \"...\"\n   185→}\n   186→```\n   187→\n   188→#### Scenario: Worker blocked on ambiguity\n   189→- **WHEN** worker encounters unclear requirement\n   190→- **THEN** worker writes `human-calls/task-001-clarification.md`\n   191→- **AND** worker exits with code 2\n   192→- **WHEN** orchestrator sees exit code 2\n   193→- **THEN** sets status to `blocked` and continues other tasks\n   194→- **WHEN** human responds\n   195→- **THEN** orchestrator re-spawns worker with human's answer\n   196→\n   197→#### Scenario: Manager reviews completed work\n   198→- **WHEN** worker exits with code 0\n   199→- **THEN** orchestrator invokes manager with review context\n   200→- **AND** manager examines git diff (not live worker)\n   201→- **THEN** manager returns merge/reject/split decision\n   202→\n   203→---\n   204→\n   205→### Requirement: Orchestrator Event Loop (Bash)\n   206→\n   207→The orchestrator SHALL implement a simple bash event loop.\n   208→\n   209→```bash\n   210→# Pseudocode\n   211→load_state() {\n   212→  CONFIG=$(cat .collab/config.json)\n   213→  TASKS=(.collab/tasks/task-*.json)\n   214→}\n   215→\n   216→spawn_manager(event_type, context) {\n   217→  claude -p \"$MANAGER_PROMPT\" --output-format json\n   218→  # Parse JSON, return action\n   219→}\n   220→\n   221→spawn_worker(task_id) {\n   222→  git worktree add \".worktrees/$task_id\" -b \"collab/$task_id\"\n   223→  claude -p \"$WORKER_PROMPT\" &\n   224→  echo $! > .collab/tasks/$task_id.pid\n   225→}\n   226→\n   227→main_loop() {\n   228→  load_state\n   229→\n   230→  # Initial planning if no tasks\n   231→  if no_tasks; then\n   232→    action=$(spawn_manager \"plan\" \"$OBJECTIVE\")\n   233→    create_task_files \"$action\"\n   234→  fi\n   235→\n   236→  # Main loop\n   237→  while true; do\n   238→    # Spawn workers up to limit\n   239→    for task in pending_tasks; do\n   240→      if active_workers < max_parallel; then\n   241→        spawn_worker \"$task\"\n   242→      fi\n   243→    done\n   244→\n   245→    # Wait for any child to exit\n   246→    wait -n  # bash waits for any background job\n   247→\n   248→    # Process exited workers\n   249→    for task in in_progress_tasks; do\n   250→      if ! kill -0 \"$task.pid\" 2>/dev/null; then\n   251→        exit_code=$?  # Get actual exit code\n   252→        handle_worker_exit \"$task\" \"$exit_code\"\n   253→      fi\n   254→    done\n   255→\n   256→    # Check if all tasks terminal\n   257→    if all_terminal; then\n   258→      generate_summary\n   259→      exit 0\n   260→    fi\n   261→  done\n   262→}\n   263→```\n   264→\n   265→#### Scenario: Parallel worker spawning\n   266→- **WHEN** 3 tasks pending and max_parallel=3\n   267→- **THEN** orchestrator spawns all 3 workers concurrently\n   268→- **WHEN** one worker exits\n   269→- **THEN** orchestrator spawns manager for review\n   270→- **AND** may spawn next pending worker if slot available\n   271→\n   272→#### Scenario: Sequential manager invocation\n   273→- **WHEN** two workers complete simultaneously\n   274→- **THEN** orchestrator queues manager invocations\n   275→- **AND** processes them one at a time\n   276→\n   277→---\n   278→\n   279→### Requirement: Health Monitoring (Simplified)\n   280→\n   281→**Worker timeout:**\n   282→- Bash `timeout` command wraps worker: `timeout ${TIMEOUT}m claude -p ...`\n   283→- Exit code 124 = timeout\n   284→\n   285→**Stall detection:**\n   286→- Orchestrator periodically checks: `git -C \"$worktree\" log -1 --format=%ct`\n   287→- No commit within `stale_threshold_minutes` = stall\n   288→- Kill worker, set status to `timeout`\n   289→\n   290→**Manager timeout:**\n   291→- `timeout ${MANAGER_TIMEOUT}m claude -p ...`\n   292→- On timeout: retry once with simplified prompt\n   293→- On retry failure: escalate to human\n   294→\n   295→#### Scenario: Worker timeout\n   296→- **WHEN** worker exceeds `worker_timeout_minutes`\n   297→- **THEN** `timeout` kills the process, exit code 124\n   298→- **AND** orchestrator sets status to `timeout`\n   299→- **AND** invokes manager for retry/escalate decision\n   300→\n   301→#### Scenario: Worker stall (no commits)\n   302→- **WHEN** worker alive but no git activity for 30 minutes\n   303→- **THEN** orchestrator kills worker\n   304→- **AND** sets status to `timeout`\n   305→\n   306→---\n   307→\n   308→### Requirement: Human-as-MCP (Direct)\n   309→\n   310→Workers and Manager SHALL interact with human directly via `human-calls/` directory.\n   311→\n   312→**Worker blocked:**\n   313→1. Worker writes `human-calls/{task-id}-{question}.md`\n   314→2. Worker exits with code 2\n   315→3. Orchestrator sets task status to `blocked`\n   316→4. Orchestrator continues other tasks\n   317→5. When human responds, orchestrator re-spawns worker\n   318→\n   319→**Manager escalates:**\n   320→1. Manager writes `human-calls/escalate-{timestamp}.md`\n   321→2. Manager returns `{\"action\": \"escalate\", ...}`\n   322→3. Orchestrator pauses session, waits for human\n   323→\n   324→**NO MCP server required** — direct file I/O.\n   325→\n   326→---\n   327→\n   328→## CLI Commands\n   329→\n   330→```bash\n   331→# Start automatic collaboration\n   332→se3 collab --daemon \"Implement auth and caching\"\n   333→\n   334→# Resume crashed session\n   335→se3 collab --resume\n   336→\n   337→# Check status\n   338→se3 collab --status\n   339→\n   340→# Abort and cleanup\n   341→se3 collab --abort\n   342→\n   343→# Manual mode (generate plan, execute manually)\n   344→se3 collab --manual \"Implement feature X\"\n   345→```\n   346→\n   347→## Configuration (se3.config.yaml)\n   348→\n   349→```yaml\n   350→collab:\n   351→  max_parallel_workers: 3\n   352→  worker_timeout_minutes: 60\n   353→  manager_timeout_minutes: 15\n   354→  stale_threshold_minutes: 30\n   355→  max_worker_attempts: 3\n   356→  max_manager_retries: 2\n   357→```\n   358→\n   359→## Design Principle: Minimize External Dependencies\n   360→\n   361→The orchestrator layer (bash scripts) SHALL minimize external tool dependencies. Python 3 is the only required runtime beyond standard POSIX tools.\n   362→\n   363→**Rationale:**\n   364→- Collab runs in diverse environments; every additional `apt install` raises the barrier to use\n   365→- SE3's tech stack is Python — reuse it rather than adding system-level dependencies\n   366→\n   367→**Current application — `jq-complete.py`:**\n   368→- Shell scripts use `$JQ_CMD` which auto-detects system `jq`, falling back to `scripts/jq-complete.py`\n   369→- The Python fallback covers the subset of jq used by the orchestrator (field access, defaults, assignment)\n   370→- It is NOT a full jq replacement — complex expressions like `select()`, `map()`, `if-then-else` are unsupported\n   371→\n   372→**Future direction:**\n   373→- When JSON processing logic in shell scripts grows complex enough to need advanced jq features, migrate that logic to Python modules instead of extending `jq-complete.py`\n   374→- Shell scripts should stay as thin orchestration glue; non-trivial data processing belongs in Python\n   375→\n   376→---\n   377→\n   378→## Migration from v2 (External Controller)\n   379→\n   380→**To be removed:**\n   381→- `tools/se3_tools/controller/` (daemon, api_server, persistence)\n   382→- `tools/se3_tools/commands/collab_v2.py`\n   383→- `scripts/mcp-collab/`\n   384→\n   385→**To keep:**\n   386→- `tools/se3_tools/commands/collab.py` (v1 bash orchestrator)\n   387→- `scripts/collab-orchestrator.sh`\n   388→- `scripts/rules-worker.md`\n   389→- `scripts/rules-manager.md`\n   390→\n   391→**Behavior change:**\n   392→- No `se3 controller` commands\n   393→- No persistent daemon process\n   394→- `--daemon` flag starts bash orchestrator in background (not Python daemon)\n   395→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"26847e8e-a8cf-4e28-8be2-13f7a7769227","uuid":"11c28c78-a4e0-42e1-bb08-ed5a6371c61b","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/data/cre/workspace/se3.0/.worktrees/remove-external-controller/openspec/specs/git-worktree-collab/spec.md","content":"# git-worktree-collab Specification (v2 - Simplified)\n\n## Purpose\n\nReplace the experimental External Controller (v2) with a simplified architecture based on the proven bash orchestrator (v1). Remove unnecessary complexity: no daemon, no HTTP API, no MCP server, no real-time manager-worker communication.\n\n**Core principle**: Git worktree-based isolation + file-based async communication only.\n\n## Architecture Overview\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  Layer 1: Orchestrator (bash)                       │\n│  - Event loop: spawn → wait → react                 │\n│  - File system is the ONLY communication channel    │\n│  - Zero AI token cost while idle                    │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│  Layer 2: Manager (claude -p)                       │\n│  - Invoked on-demand when decisions needed          │\n│  - Stateless: reads .collab/, writes decisions      │\n│  - NO real-time communication with workers          │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│  Layer 3: Workers (claude -p)                       │\n│  - Isolated in git worktrees                        │\n│  - Independent full context window                  │\n│  - Commit & exit — process exit = task complete     │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n## Key Design Decisions\n\n### 1. No Daemon, No API, No MCP\n\n**REMOVED from v2:**\n- ❌ Python daemon process (`daemon.py`)\n- ❌ HTTP API server (`api_server.py`)\n- ❌ MCP server for manager-worker communication (`mcp-collab/server`)\n- ❌ Real-time progress reporting\n\n**RATIONALE:**\n- Bash orchestrator is sufficient — it spawns processes and waits for exit\n- File system communication is simpler and more reliable\n- Manager and Worker do NOT need to communicate during worker execution\n- Worker progress is tracked via git commits, not real-time reports\n\n### 2. Async Communication Only\n\n**Communication pattern:**\n```\nManager creates Task File ──► Worker reads Task File (at start)\n                              Worker works independently\n                              Worker writes result (git commit + exit)\nWorker exit triggers ───────► Manager reads result (at end)\n```\n\n**NO communication during worker execution:**\n- Manager does not monitor worker progress\n- Worker does not ask manager questions mid-task\n- Worker blocks/writes human-calls/ directly if human needed\n\n**RATIONALE:**\n- Git worktree paradigm: branch is isolation boundary\n- Commit history is the progress indicator\n- Human calls go directly to human-calls/, not through manager\n\n### 3. Simplified Health Monitoring\n\n**Worker health:**\n- Process timeout via bash `timeout` command\n- Git commit activity check (orchestrator polls periodically)\n- NO heartbeat/MCP required\n\n**Manager health:**\n- Timeout on `claude -p` invocation\n- JSON validation with retry\n\n**Orchestrator health:**\n- NO watchdog layer — orchestrator crash = session ends\n- State persistence in `.collab/` allows manual resume\n\n## Requirements\n\n### Requirement: Three-Layer Architecture (Simplified)\n\nThe system SHALL use a three-layer architecture with bash orchestrator, manager (claude -p), and workers (claude -p).\n\n**Orchestrator** (Layer 1):\n- Pure bash script — no daemon, no resident process\n- Spawns manager/worker via `claude -p`, waits for exit\n- Reads task files, updates status, makes spawn decisions\n- All state in `.collab/` files — orchestrator is stateless\n\n**Manager** (Layer 2):\n- Invoked via `claude -p` for specific decisions only\n- Reads `.collab/` state, returns JSON decision\n- Does NOT communicate with running workers\n- Exits after returning decision\n\n**Workers** (Layer 3):\n- Each runs as independent `claude -p` in git worktree\n- Full context window, no shared state pressure\n- Commits to branch, exits when done (exit code = result)\n- If blocked: write to `human-calls/`, exit with code 2\n\n#### Scenario: Event-driven orchestrator loop\n- **WHEN** orchestrator starts\n- **THEN** it spawns manager for initial planning\n- **WHEN** manager returns task list\n- **THEN** orchestrator spawns workers up to `max_parallel_workers`\n- **WHEN** any worker exits\n- **THEN** orchestrator spawns manager for review/failure-handling\n- **WHEN** all tasks terminal\n- **THEN** orchestrator exits\n\n#### Scenario: Stateless recovery\n- **WHEN** orchestrator is restarted with `--resume`\n- **THEN** it reads `.collab/config.json` and `.collab/tasks/*.json`\n- **AND** resumes the event loop from current state\n\n---\n\n### Requirement: Task File Protocol (Unchanged)\n\nThe system SHALL use JSON task files in `.collab/tasks/` as the single source of truth.\n\n**Task lifecycle**: `pending` → `in_progress` → (`done` | `failed` | `blocked` | `timeout`)\n\n**Task file format**: Same as v1 (see original spec for full schema)\n\nKey fields:\n- `id`, `status`, `branch`, `worktree`\n- `prompt`: Full worker prompt\n- `worker_pid`: Set by orchestrator when spawning\n- `worker_exit_code`: Set by orchestrator on exit\n- `health.attempts`: Retry counter\n- `health.timeout_minutes`: Timeout setting\n\n**Collaboration config** (`.collab/config.json`):\n```json\n{\n  \"session_id\": \"collab-20260215-100000\",\n  \"objective\": \"Implement features X, Y, Z\",\n  \"base_branch\": \"master\",\n  \"max_parallel_workers\": 3,\n  \"worker_timeout_minutes\": 60,\n  \"manager_timeout_minutes\": 15,\n  \"status\": \"active\"\n}\n```\n\n#### Scenario: Task persistence\n- **WHEN** orchestrator spawns a worker\n- **THEN** it writes `worker_pid` to task file\n- **WHEN** worker exits\n- **THEN** orchestrator records `worker_exit_code` and updates `status`\n\n---\n\n### Requirement: Manager-Worker Async Boundary\n\nManager and Worker SHALL NOT communicate during worker execution.\n\n**Worker prompt includes:**\n- Task description\n- Spec references\n- Rules (from `rules-worker.md`)\n- Instruction: \"Work independently. Commit your changes. Exit when done.\"\n\n**Worker blocked/needs help:**\n- Worker writes to `human-calls/` directly\n- Worker exits with code 2 (blocked)\n- Orchestrator sets status to `blocked`\n- Human response processed in next orchestrator loop\n\n**Manager decisions (JSON response):**\n```json\n{\n  \"action\": \"plan|merge|reject|retry|split|escalate|complete\",\n  \"tasks\": [...],\n  \"target_task\": \"task-001\",\n  \"merge_branch\": \"collab/feature-x\",\n  \"retry_prompt\": \"...\",\n  \"reason\": \"...\",\n  \"summary\": \"...\"\n}\n```\n\n#### Scenario: Worker blocked on ambiguity\n- **WHEN** worker encounters unclear requirement\n- **THEN** worker writes `human-calls/task-001-clarification.md`\n- **AND** worker exits with code 2\n- **WHEN** orchestrator sees exit code 2\n- **THEN** sets status to `blocked` and continues other tasks\n- **WHEN** human responds\n- **THEN** orchestrator re-spawns worker with human's answer\n\n#### Scenario: Manager reviews completed work\n- **WHEN** worker exits with code 0\n- **THEN** orchestrator invokes manager with review context\n- **AND** manager examines git diff (not live worker)\n- **THEN** manager returns merge/reject/split decision\n\n---\n\n### Requirement: Orchestrator Event Loop (Bash)\n\nThe orchestrator SHALL implement a simple bash event loop.\n\n```bash\n# Pseudocode\nload_state() {\n  CONFIG=$(cat .collab/config.json)\n  TASKS=(.collab/tasks/task-*.json)\n}\n\nspawn_manager(event_type, context) {\n  claude -p \"$MANAGER_PROMPT\" --output-format json\n  # Parse JSON, return action\n}\n\nspawn_worker(task_id) {\n  git worktree add \".worktrees/$task_id\" -b \"collab/$task_id\"\n  claude -p \"$WORKER_PROMPT\" &\n  echo $! > .collab/tasks/$task_id.pid\n}\n\nmain_loop() {\n  load_state\n\n  # Initial planning if no tasks\n  if no_tasks; then\n    action=$(spawn_manager \"plan\" \"$OBJECTIVE\")\n    create_task_files \"$action\"\n  fi\n\n  # Main loop\n  while true; do\n    # Spawn workers up to limit\n    for task in pending_tasks; do\n      if active_workers < max_parallel; then\n        spawn_worker \"$task\"\n      fi\n    done\n\n    # Wait for any child to exit\n    wait -n  # bash waits for any background job\n\n    # Process exited workers\n    for task in in_progress_tasks; do\n      if ! kill -0 \"$task.pid\" 2>/dev/null; then\n        exit_code=$?  # Get actual exit code\n        handle_worker_exit \"$task\" \"$exit_code\"\n      fi\n    done\n\n    # Check if all tasks terminal\n    if all_terminal; then\n      generate_summary\n      exit 0\n    fi\n  done\n}\n```\n\n#### Scenario: Parallel worker spawning\n- **WHEN** 3 tasks pending and max_parallel=3\n- **THEN** orchestrator spawns all 3 workers concurrently\n- **WHEN** one worker exits\n- **THEN** orchestrator spawns manager for review\n- **AND** may spawn next pending worker if slot available\n\n#### Scenario: Sequential manager invocation\n- **WHEN** two workers complete simultaneously\n- **THEN** orchestrator queues manager invocations\n- **AND** processes them one at a time\n\n---\n\n### Requirement: Health Monitoring (Simplified)\n\n**Worker timeout:**\n- Bash `timeout` command wraps worker: `timeout ${TIMEOUT}m claude -p ...`\n- Exit code 124 = timeout\n\n**Stall detection:**\n- Orchestrator periodically checks: `git -C \"$worktree\" log -1 --format=%ct`\n- No commit within `stale_threshold_minutes` = stall\n- Kill worker, set status to `timeout`\n\n**Manager timeout:**\n- `timeout ${MANAGER_TIMEOUT}m claude -p ...`\n- On timeout: retry once with simplified prompt\n- On retry failure: escalate to human\n\n#### Scenario: Worker timeout\n- **WHEN** worker exceeds `worker_timeout_minutes`\n- **THEN** `timeout` kills the process, exit code 124\n- **AND** orchestrator sets status to `timeout`\n- **AND** invokes manager for retry/escalate decision\n\n#### Scenario: Worker stall (no commits)\n- **WHEN** worker alive but no git activity for 30 minutes\n- **THEN** orchestrator kills worker\n- **AND** sets status to `timeout`\n\n---\n\n### Requirement: Human-as-MCP (Direct)\n\nWorkers and Manager SHALL interact with human directly via `human-calls/` directory.\n\n**Worker blocked:**\n1. Worker writes `human-calls/{task-id}-{question}.md`\n2. Worker exits with code 2\n3. Orchestrator sets task status to `blocked`\n4. Orchestrator continues other tasks\n5. When human responds, orchestrator re-spawns worker\n\n**Manager escalates:**\n1. Manager writes `human-calls/escalate-{timestamp}.md`\n2. Manager returns `{\"action\": \"escalate\", ...}`\n3. Orchestrator pauses session, waits for human\n\n**NO MCP server required** — direct file I/O.\n\n---\n\n## CLI Commands\n\n```bash\n# Start automatic collaboration\nse3 collab --daemon \"Implement auth and caching\"\n\n# Resume crashed session\nse3 collab --resume\n\n# Check status\nse3 collab --status\n\n# Abort and cleanup\nse3 collab --abort\n\n# Manual mode (generate plan, execute manually)\nse3 collab --manual \"Implement feature X\"\n```\n\n## Configuration (se3.config.yaml)\n\n```yaml\ncollab:\n  max_parallel_workers: 3\n  worker_timeout_minutes: 60\n  manager_timeout_minutes: 15\n  stale_threshold_minutes: 30\n  max_worker_attempts: 3\n  max_manager_retries: 2\n```\n\n## Design Principle: Minimize External Dependencies\n\nThe orchestrator layer (bash scripts) SHALL minimize external tool dependencies. Python 3 is the only required runtime beyond standard POSIX tools.\n\n**Rationale:**\n- Collab runs in diverse environments; every additional `apt install` raises the barrier to use\n- SE3's tech stack is Python — reuse it rather than adding system-level dependencies\n\n**Current application — `jq-complete.py`:**\n- Shell scripts use `$JQ_CMD` which auto-detects system `jq`, falling back to `scripts/jq-complete.py`\n- The Python fallback covers the subset of jq used by the orchestrator (field access, defaults, assignment)\n- It is NOT a full jq replacement — complex expressions like `select()`, `map()`, `if-then-else` are unsupported\n\n**Future direction:**\n- When JSON processing logic in shell scripts grows complex enough to need advanced jq features, migrate that logic to Python modules instead of extending `jq-complete.py`\n- Shell scripts should stay as thin orchestration glue; non-trivial data processing belongs in Python\n\n---\n\n## Migration from v2 (External Controller)\n\n**To be removed:**\n- `tools/se3_tools/controller/` (daemon, api_server, persistence)\n- `tools/se3_tools/commands/collab_v2.py`\n- `scripts/mcp-collab/`\n\n**To keep:**\n- `tools/se3_tools/commands/collab.py` (v1 bash orchestrator)\n- `scripts/collab-orchestrator.sh`\n- `scripts/rules-worker.md`\n- `scripts/rules-manager.md`\n\n**Behavior change:**\n- No `se3 controller` commands\n- No persistent daemon process\n- `--daemon` flag starts bash orchestrator in background (not Python daemon)\n","numLines":395,"startLine":1,"totalLines":395}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"tool_8oXU6lNn9ZNT5yBsQhRGnVmD","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→openapi: 3.0.0\n     2→info:\n     3→  title: SE3 External Controller\n     4→  version: 1.0.0\n     5→  description: |\n     6→    External control daemon for SE3 framework.\n     7→    Manages Claude sessions, auto-commit, and multi-agent collaboration.\n     8→\n     9→paths:\n    10→  # Session Management\n    11→  /session/start:\n    12→    post:\n    13→      summary: Start new interactive session\n    14→      requestBody:\n    15→        content:\n    16→          application/json:\n    17→            schema:\n    18→              type: object\n    19→              properties:\n    20→                objective:\n    21→                  type: string\n    22→                mode:\n    23→                  type: string\n    24→                  enum: [interactive, worker, manager]\n    25→      responses:\n    26→        200:\n    27→          description: Session started\n    28→          content:\n    29→            application/json:\n    30→              schema:\n    31→                type: object\n    32→                properties:\n    33→                  session_id:\n    34→                    type: string\n    35→                  pid:\n    36→                    type: integer\n    37→\n    38→  /session/stop:\n    39→    post:\n    40→      summary: Stop session with commit\n    41→      requestBody:\n    42→        content:\n    43→          application/json:\n    44→            schema:\n    45→              type: object\n    46→              properties:\n    47→                force:\n    48→                  type: boolean\n    49→                skip_commit:\n    50→                  type: boolean\n    51→      responses:\n    52→        200:\n    53→          description: Session stopped\n    54→\n    55→  /session/status:\n    56→    get:\n    57→      summary: Get current session status\n    58→      responses:\n    59→        200:\n    60→          description: Session status\n    61→          content:\n    62→            application/json:\n    63→              schema:\n    64→                type: object\n    65→                properties:\n    66→                  session_id:\n    67→                    type: string\n    68→                  status:\n    69→                    type: string\n    70→                    enum: [active, paused, stopping]\n    71→                  pending_commits:\n    72→                    type: boolean\n    73→\n    74→  # Auto-Commit Control\n    75→  /commit/trigger:\n    76→    post:\n    77→      summary: Trigger immediate commit\n    78→      requestBody:\n    79→        content:\n    80→          application/json:\n    81→            schema:\n    82→              type: object\n    83→              properties:\n    84→                reason:\n    85→                  type: string\n    86→                message:\n    87→                  type: string\n    88→      responses:\n    89→        200:\n    90→          description: Commit result\n    91→\n    92→  /commit/config:\n    93→    get:\n    94→      summary: Get auto-commit configuration\n    95→      responses:\n    96→        200:\n    97→          description: Configuration\n    98→    put:\n    99→      summary: Update auto-commit configuration\n   100→      requestBody:\n   101→        content:\n   102→          application/json:\n   103→            schema:\n   104→              type: object\n   105→              properties:\n   106→                silence_timeout:\n   107→                  type: integer\n   108→                  description: Seconds of inactivity before auto-commit\n   109→                commit_on_test_pass:\n   110→                  type: boolean\n   111→                commit_on_session_end:\n   112→                  type: boolean\n   113→\n   114→  # Collaboration\n   115→  /collab/start:\n   116→    post:\n   117→      summary: Start collaboration session\n   118→      requestBody:\n   119→        content:\n   120→          application/json:\n   121→            schema:\n   122→              type: object\n   123→              properties:\n   124→                objective:\n   125→                  type: string\n   126→                max_workers:\n   127→                  type: integer\n   128→      responses:\n   129→        200:\n   130→          description: Collaboration started\n   131→\n   132→  /collab/spawn:\n   133→    post:\n   134→      summary: Spawn worker/manager process\n   135→      requestBody:\n   136→        content:\n   137→          application/json:\n   138→            schema:\n   139→              type: object\n   140→              properties:\n   141→                role:\n   142→                  type: string\n   143→                  enum: [worker, manager]\n   144→                task_id:\n   145→                  type: string\n   146→                prompt:\n   147→                  type: string\n   148→      responses:\n   149→        200:\n   150→          description: Process spawned\n   151→\n   152→components:\n   153→  schemas:\n   154→    Session:\n   155→      type: object\n   156→      properties:\n   157→        session_id:\n   158→          type: string\n   159→        pid:\n   160→          type: integer\n   161→        mode:\n   162→          type: string\n   163→        start_time:\n   164→          type: string\n   165→          format: date-time\n   166→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"26847e8e-a8cf-4e28-8be2-13f7a7769227","uuid":"9da7c935-9d23-4dc6-9109-d548cc54c91a","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/data/cre/workspace/se3.0/.worktrees/remove-external-controller/openspec/specs/se3-controller/spec.yaml","content":"openapi: 3.0.0\ninfo:\n  title: SE3 External Controller\n  version: 1.0.0\n  description: |\n    External control daemon for SE3 framework.\n    Manages Claude sessions, auto-commit, and multi-agent collaboration.\n\npaths:\n  # Session Management\n  /session/start:\n    post:\n      summary: Start new interactive session\n      requestBody:\n        content:\n          application/json:\n            schema:\n              type: object\n              properties:\n                objective:\n                  type: string\n                mode:\n                  type: string\n                  enum: [interactive, worker, manager]\n      responses:\n        200:\n          description: Session started\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                type: object\n                properties:\n                  session_id:\n                    type: string\n                  pid:\n                    type: integer\n\n  /session/stop:\n    post:\n      summary: Stop session with commit\n      requestBody:\n        content:\n          application/json:\n            schema:\n              type: object\n              properties:\n                force:\n                  type: boolean\n                skip_commit:\n                  type: boolean\n      responses:\n        200:\n          description: Session stopped\n\n  /session/status:\n    get:\n      summary: Get current session status\n      responses:\n        200:\n          description: Session status\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                type: object\n                properties:\n                  session_id:\n                    type: string\n                  status:\n                    type: string\n                    enum: [active, paused, stopping]\n                  pending_commits:\n                    type: boolean\n\n  # Auto-Commit Control\n  /commit/trigger:\n    post:\n      summary: Trigger immediate commit\n      requestBody:\n        content:\n          application/json:\n            schema:\n              type: object\n              properties:\n                reason:\n                  type: string\n                message:\n                  type: string\n      responses:\n        200:\n          description: Commit result\n\n  /commit/config:\n    get:\n      summary: Get auto-commit configuration\n      responses:\n        200:\n          description: Configuration\n    put:\n      summary: Update auto-commit configuration\n      requestBody:\n        content:\n          application/json:\n            schema:\n              type: object\n              properties:\n                silence_timeout:\n                  type: integer\n                  description: Seconds of inactivity before auto-commit\n                commit_on_test_pass:\n                  type: boolean\n                commit_on_session_end:\n                  type: boolean\n\n  # Collaboration\n  /collab/start:\n    post:\n      summary: Start collaboration session\n      requestBody:\n        content:\n          application/json:\n            schema:\n              type: object\n              properties:\n                objective:\n                  type: string\n                max_workers:\n                  type: integer\n      responses:\n        200:\n          description: Collaboration started\n\n  /collab/spawn:\n    post:\n      summary: Spawn worker/manager process\n      requestBody:\n        content:\n          application/json:\n            schema:\n              type: object\n              properties:\n                role:\n                  type: string\n                  enum: [worker, manager]\n                task_id:\n                  type: string\n                prompt:\n                  type: string\n      responses:\n        200:\n          description: Process spawned\n\ncomponents:\n  schemas:\n    Session:\n      type: object\n      properties:\n        session_id:\n          type: string\n        pid:\n          type: integer\n        mode:\n          type: string\n        start_time:\n          type: string\n          format: date-time\n","numLines":166,"startLine":1,"totalLines":166}}}
